      "body": "## Motivation\n\nAsync readback callbacks run on a new thread, which starts with gradients enabled instead of the scheduler's no-grad/inference-mode policy. A callback raising `SystemExit` also currently signals successful completion before killing the worker, leaving later copies unresolved.\n\n## Modifications\n\nApply `DynamicGradMode` around each copy and record `BaseException` failures through the existing `HostCopyDone` error path, so consumers reject invalid results and subsequent copies can finish. Add two regression cases to the existing worker GPU fixture.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Both new cases fail against main at `0dc6de2e74e999464b5e63a9a059db2e4e0518a3` before the runtime fix.\n- `python -m pytest test/registered/unit/managers/test_async_d2h_copy_worker.py -q`: **10 passed, 6 subtests passed** on a CUDA GPU.\n- Same file with `SGLANG_ENABLE_TORCH_INFERENCE_MODE=true`: **10 passed, 6 subtests passed**.\n- These cover exact readback values, producer-stream ordering, scheduler routing, error propagation, continued processing after failure, and both grad policies.\n- No model-serving accuracy evaluation was run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo serving benchmark was run; this fixes worker context and error handling. The existing GPU readback tests passed under both grad policies.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add regression tests that fail before the fix.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #39186060824](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39186060824)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39186060768](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39186060768)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39186060862](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39186060862)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
